{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the Valley of Siddim had pits.</b> Rashi's comment from midrash aggadah: the mud in them was burning, as it is written <b>ועמק השדים</b> in the sense of lime (סיד). As it says elsewhere, ״ושדת אותם בשיד״ with a shin." "<b>Pits, pits of clay.</b> The bet has a segol vowel and the alef has a hatef-segol." "<b>And they fell there.</b> Of their own will they fell in order to hide there and save their lives. This is the sense of ״על פני כל אחיו נפל,״ for the pits mentioned were not full of wet mud, but are so called because earth is taken out of them to make mud."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:12.409148789Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}